WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.533
Rome, 100 BCE. Julius Caesar is born.

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:05.100
A patrician family. An ambitious future.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.433
59 BCE: Caesar becomes consul.

00:00:08.433 --> 00:00:12.267
Allies Pompey and Crassus help him rise.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:17.267
58–50 BCE: wars in Gaul bring wealth and power.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:26.400
Conquest also brings death and enslavement.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.067
49 BCE: Caesar reaches the Rubicon.

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:39.067
He crosses with his army. Civil war follows.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:42.233
He reforms Rome's calendar.

00:00:42.233 --> 00:00:45.400
44 BCE: dictator for life. Not an emperor.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.067
15 March, 44 BCE. Senators surround Caesar.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:51.167
They kill him. His death does not end the crisis.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:54.833
More civil wars follow.

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:59.167
27 BCE: his heir Octavian becomes Augustus.
